<title>FRANCE: New York top destination for air cargo exports.</title>
<headline>New York top destination for air cargo exports.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Paris airports authority, the Aeroports de Paris (ADP), said New York was the top destination for exports traffic from Charles de Gaulle and Orly Airports in the first eleven months of 1996.</p>
<p>The top ten destinations for ADP exports between January and November 1996 and the percentage change on the same period in 1995, were as follows:</p>
<p> 1  New York	   35,625 tonnes  down 17.7pct</p>
<p> 2  Chicago	    25,622 tonnes  up   14.2</p>
<p> 3  Tokyo		24,415 tonnes  down 10.6</p>
<p> 4  Hong Kong	  22,734 tonnes  up    3.6</p>
<p> 5  Mexico City	11,132 tonnes  up   30.7</p>
<p> 6  Sao Paulo	  11,115 tonnes  down  7.2</p>
<p> 7  Montreal	   11,009 tonnes  down 18.6</p>
<p> 8  Los Angeles	10,890 tonnes  up    2.3</p>
<p> 9  Miami		 8,535 tonnes  up   94.4</p>
<p> 10 Dubai		 8,776 tonnes  down  2.5</p>
<p>- Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+44 171 542 5017</p>
</text>
